{"qid":"Q5362837","names":["Emirate of Jabal Shammar"],"title":"Emirate of Jabal Shammar","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Emirate of Jabal Shammar was an Arabian state centered on Hail in the Najd highlands, founded by Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Rashid around 1836 when the Rashidi clan secured dominance over the mountain region following the collapse of the first Saudi emirate. Under Muhammad ibn Rashid (r. 1872–1897) the emirate reached its maximum power, occupying Riyadh in 1891 and temporarily displacing the Al Saud into Kuwaiti exile, making the Rashidis the pre-eminent power in central Arabia. The emirate declined rapidly after Muhammad ibn Rashid's death; successive succession disputes weakened it, and Ibn Saud recaptured Riyadh in 1902, gradually encircling Hail until the emirate's final surrender in 1921.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The emirate's territorial extent is approximately known from British consular reports and Arabian travel literature (Doughty, Palgrave, Ibn Bishr), but the steppe frontiers with tribal confederacies were fluid and contested rather than fixed.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Rashidi dynasty","url":"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Rashidi-dynasty"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Emirate of Jabal Shammar","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Jabal_Shammar"}],"britannica":"place/Jabal-Shammar","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Emirate of Jabal Shammar","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Abdullah ibn Ali Al Rashid","nativeName":"عبد الله بن علي الرشيد","roman":"ʿAbdallāh ibn ʿAlī al-Rashīd","start":1836,"end":1848,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qi